yoloctl local patch 0006: an attachments-ended record beside the canonical main-process exit marker.

After the canonical main process exits, the supervisor persists its exit
marker, reports the exit, then waits for terminal delivery to drain
(drain_main_terminal_delivery): every openshell-main attachment present at the
exit has ended. In russh 0.64 that means its SSH connection has ended: the
server closes the channel after the exit status, so a client's channel close
alone does not end the attachment. None attached ends the wait at once.

When that wait completes and an exit marker path is configured, the supervisor
now also writes `main-attachments-ended` in the marker's directory,
owner-only and atomically, with the content `ended` and a newline. It states
only that no client is attached any more; it does not tell completion from
abandonment. A wait cancelled by shutdown writes nothing; a write failure is
logged and nothing else changes. The exit marker, its timing and attachment
accounting are unchanged; there is no new flag and no timer. A reader that
ends on this file needs its own bound.

